From: PowOS
Subject: xwayland/present: don't wait on the wait fence again after the copy

A copy presentation is executed twice: once to copy (then copy_executed is set
and a vblank is queued for crtc_msc + 1), and again at that MSC to send the
completion (present_execute_post). The second pass went through
present_execute_wait() again, which re-checks the request's wait fence.

By then the client has the pixmap back (the idle notify was sent with the copy)
and may have reused the buffer: its fence is reset for the next frame. The
completion pass then waits on a fence that belongs to a later frame, becomes the
window's blocking_event, and every later request queues behind it - the client
runs out of back buffers and blocks in dri3_find_back forever.

Mesa normally presents without a wait fence, which hides this; the KGSL Mesa
build (Adreno, Android) passes one with every present. Seen with swap interval 0
(vblank_mode=0 glxgears: no frames; Chromium/Steam's web UI: GPU process hung
until its watchdog killed it every 30 s).

Nothing is left to wait for once the copy is done: skip the wait checks then.
---
 hw/xwayland/xwayland-present.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/xwayland/xwayland-present.c b/hw/xwayland/xwayland-present.c
--- a/hw/xwayland/xwayland-present.c
+++ b/hw/xwayland/xwayland-present.c
@@ -1050,8 +1050,9 @@
     }
 
 retry:
-    if (present_execute_wait(vblank, crtc_msc) ||
-        xwl_present_wait_acquire_fence_avail(xwl_screen, vblank)) {
+    if (!event->copy_executed &&
+        (present_execute_wait(vblank, crtc_msc) ||
+         xwl_present_wait_acquire_fence_avail(xwl_screen, vblank))) {
         if (!notify_only)
             /* block execution of subsequent requests until this request is ready */
             xwl_present_window->blocking_event = event->vblank.event_id;
